				"Overview",
				"The roughly 200 species of ruminants include both domestic and wild species. Ruminating mammals include [[Cattle|cattle]], all domesticated and wild bovines, [[Goat|goats]], [[Sheep|sheep]], [[Giraffe|giraffes]], [[Deer|deer]], [[Gazelle|gazelles]], and [[Antelope|antelopes]]. It has also been suggested that notoungulates also relied on rumination, as opposed to other atlantogenatans that rely on the more typical hindgut fermentation, though this is not entirely certain. Ruminants represent the most diverse group of living [[Ungulate|ungulates]]. The suborder Ruminantia includes six different families: Tragulidae, Giraffidae, Antilocapridae, Cervidae, Moschidae, and [[Bovidae]].",
