		summary = '**Salmonidae** is a [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] of [[Actinopterygii|ray-finned fish]], the only extant member of the [[Order (taxonomy)|suborder]] **Salmonoidei**, consisting of 11 extant [[Genus|genera]] and over 200 [[Species|species]] collectively known as "**salmonids**" or "**salmonoids**". The family includes [[Salmon|salmon]] (both Atlantic and Pacific species), [[Trout|trout]] (both ocean-going and landlocked), char, graylings, freshwater whitefishes, taimens and lenoks, all coldwater mid-level predatory fish that inhabit the [[Subarctic|subarctic]] and cool [[Temperate climate|temperate]] waters of the [[Northern Hemisphere]]. The Atlantic salmon (Salmo salar), whose [[Latin]] name became that of its [[Genus|genus]] Salmo, is also the eponym of the family and order names.',
		sections = {
