		summary = "**Scale insects** are small [[Insect|insects]] of the [[Order (taxonomy)|order]] [[Hemiptera]], suborder Sternorrhyncha. Adult females typically have soft bodies and no limbs, and are concealed underneath domed scales, extruding quantities of wax for protection. Some species are hermaphroditic, with a combined ovotestis instead of separate ovaries and testes. Males, in the species where they occur, have legs and sometimes wings, and resemble small flies. Scale insects are [[Herbivore|herbivores]], piercing plant tissues with their mouthparts and remaining in one place, feeding on sap. The excess fluid they imbibe is secreted as honeydew on which sooty mold tends to grow.",
